    "title": "DnD 5.5 Fey Pact Feat Guide",
    "authors": [
      "T.E. \"RPGBOT\" Kamstra"
    ],
    "sourceFile": "source/rpgbot-958ce1756ba45cd7-7c685be633d09134.html",
    "evidence": "Owner explicitly requested the RPGbot full-text crawl on 2026-09-29"
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DnD 5.5’s "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Fey Pact feat",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/feats/2097418-fey-pact"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", introduced in “D&D Beyond Drops”, has the same pact magic flavor as the Archfey Warlock without the class levels. It’s not marked as an Origin Feat, so it must be taken as a normal feat or as part of the "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Pact Seeker",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/backgrounds/546535-pact-seeker"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " background, which allows you to pick any one “Planar Pact” feat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fey Pact It gives you a little taste of Fey magic and charm, providing features similar to Origin Feats like Skilled and Magic Initiate. The feat doesn’t focus on any one thing, which makes it hard to build around on its own. But if you just need True Strike, such as for a Rogue building around a mental ability score, Fey Pact may be exactly what you need. Because there are useful Cantrip choices which don’t rely on your stats (Just Guidance. It’s a short list.), this can fit on a wide variety of builds, but will favor Charisma-based-builds looking to capitalize on Honeyed Words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fey Pact is required for the "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Fey Sentinel",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/feats/fey-sentinel/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Fey Tormentor",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/feats/fey-tormentor/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " feats."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fey Pact received errata in the August 2026 Drops, updated Honeyed Words to only consume its single daily use on success."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fey-bond",
      "heading": "Fey Bond",
      "sourceAnchor": "fey-bond",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fey-bond-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "One language and proficiency in Nature."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fey-cantrips",
      "heading": "Fey Cantrips",
      "sourceAnchor": "fey-cantrips",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fey-cantrips-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two Cantrips, but one of them is Druidcraft, which is fun but largely useless. Your second Cantrip can be any Cantrip from the "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Divination or Enchantment",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/spells?filter-search=&filter-level=0&filter-school=5&filter-school=6&filter-verbal=&filter-somatic=&filter-material=&filter-concentration=&filter-ritual=&filter-partnered-content=f"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " school. As of this writing, that includes exactly 6 Cantrips, but does include some really great options including Mind Sliver, Guidance, True Strike, and Vicious Mockery."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-honeyed-words",
      "heading": "Honeyed Words",
      "sourceAnchor": "honeyed-words",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-honeyed-words-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you’re your party’s Face and you don’t have a feature like the Rogue’s Reliable Talent of the Eloquence Bard’s Silver Tongue, this is a useful way to resuce truly horrendous rolls for Deception and Persuasion. It’s great, and it’s not wasted if you still fail."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-5",
      "heading": "What are DnD Beyond Drops?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-5-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Starting in April of 2026, DnD Beyond Drops aim to release monthly content for DnD 5.5 accessible exclusively to users with a paid subscription to DnD Beyond. The included character options are shareable with subscriptions that allow content sharing. For more information, see the official "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "D&D Beyond Drops FAQ",
              "href": "https://dndbeyond-support.wizards.com/hc/en-us/sections/48937182240404"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". The developers also posted "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Reddit AMA discussing Drops",
              "href": "https://www.reddit.com/r/dndbeyond/comments/1t6f0pe/ama_with_ddb_executive_producer_drops_product/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " when they were announced."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-5-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We saw the first round of errata for Drops in "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "August of 2026",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2222-d-d-beyonds-august-drop-sewers-and-treasures?icid_medium=organic&icid_source=homepage_drops&icid_campaign=2026_drops&icid_content=2026_hype"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", so it appears that WotC plans to continue supporting Drops and to update the published content."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
